{
  "id": "illuminance___recommended_light_levels",
  "title": "Illuminance - Recommended Light Levels",
  "description": "Light Level or Illuminance is the total luminous flux incident on a surface per unit area. This tool provides recommended light levels for various indoor work spaces and outdoor conditions, along with calculation capabilities.",
  "type": "chart-table",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Illuminance - Recommended Light Levels\n\nLight Level or Illuminance is the total luminous flux incident on a surface per unit area (E = Φ / A, where E is illuminance in lux, Φ is luminous flux in lumens, and A is area in m²).\n\n### Measuring Units\n- **Lux (lx)**: 1 lumen per square meter (metric SI system)\n- **Foot candle (ftcd)**: 1 lumen per square foot (Imperial system)\n- **Conversion**: 1 lux = 0.0929 foot candle; 1 foot candle = 10.752 lux"
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Activity",
        "Illuminance (lx)"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Public areas with dark surroundings",
          "20 - 50"
        ],
        [
          "Simple orientation for short visits",
          "50 - 100"
        ],
        [
          "Areas with traffic and corridors (stairways, escalators, lifts, storage)",
          "100"
        ],
        [
          "Working areas where visual tasks are only occasionally performed",
          "100 - 150"
        ],
        [
          "Warehouses, homes, theaters, archives, loading bays",
          "150"
        ],
        [
          "Coffee break room, technical facilities, waiting rooms",
          "200"
        ],
        [
          "Easy office work",
          "250"
        ],
        [
          "Class rooms",
          "300"
        ],
        [
          "Normal office work, PC work, study library, groceries, kitchens, auditoriums",
          "500"
        ],
        [
          "Supermarkets, mechanical workshops, office landscapes",
          "750"
        ],
        [
          "Normal drawing work, detailed mechanical workshops, operation theaters",
          "1000"
        ],
        [
          "Detailed drawing work, very detailed mechanical works, electronic workshops",
          "1500 - 2000"
        ],
        [
          "Performance of visual tasks of low contrast and very small size",
          "2000 - 5000"
        ],
        [
          "Performance of very prolonged and exacting visual tasks",
          "5000 - 10000"
        ],
        [
          "Performance of very special visual tasks of extremely low contrast",
          "10000 - 20000"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "num_lamps",
          "label": "Number of Lamps",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 10,
          "unit": "pcs"
        },
        {
          "id": "lumens_per_lamp",
          "label": "Lumens per Lamp",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 10600,
          "unit": "lm"
        },
        {
          "id": "area",
          "label": "Area",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 50,
          "unit": "m²"
        },
        {
          "id": "utilization_coefficient",
          "label": "Coefficient of Utilization (Cu)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 0.6,
          "unit": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "light_loss_factor",
          "label": "Light Loss Factor (LLF)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 0.8,
          "unit": ""
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "total_lumens",
          "label": "Total Lumens",
          "formula": "inputs.num_lamps * inputs.lumens_per_lamp",
          "unit": "lm",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "illuminance",
          "label": "Illuminance (Lux)",
          "formula": "(inputs.num_lamps * inputs.lumens_per_lamp * inputs.utilization_coefficient * inputs.light_loss_factor) / inputs.area",
          "unit": "lx",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Condition",
        "Illuminance (ftcd)",
        "Illuminance (lux)"
      ],
